# ── Delivery boundary ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `git archive` (the clean-export / hand-off tool) OMITS files with `export-ignore`.
# These stay TRACKED in the monorepo but never appear in an export artifact.
#
# `work/` is strictly private — the dev's real lab (sprints, notes, business data). It
# must never reach a user. `method/` defaults to internal too; to SELL `method`, delete
# its line below AND add a `method` product entry to the a-la-carte CLI registry.
#
# NOTE: export-ignore only guards `git archive`. It does NOT protect a raw `git clone`
# / repo hand-off (that ships everything, incl. history) — so NEVER deliver by handing
# over the repo. Deliver only by allowlist: the CLI copy, or `git archive`. The delivery
# canary (scripts/delivery-canary.mjs, in `verify` + CI) enforces this.
#
# Patterns need `/**` (a bare `dir/` does not match files beneath it for attributes).

work/**                  export-ignore
method/**                export-ignore
**/scratch/**            export-ignore
**/settings.local.json   export-ignore
.env                     export-ignore
